[{"component_name":"Binding Seal","exact_source_excerpt":"### Binding Seal
A Binding Seal restrains or compels a spirit.
Binding Seal is Restricted or Forbidden in many orthodox sects unless used to contain hostile spirits, seal plague spirits, imprison murderous ghosts, restrain demons, secure a battlefield threat, or protect civilians.
To place a Binding Seal on an unwilling spirit, the spirit must be one of the following:
- defeated;
- restrained;
- trapped in a vessel;
- inside a prepared circle, shrine, formation, body, or object;
- reduced to 0 Hit Points or equivalent spiritual collapse;
- willingly accepting punishment;
- unable to flee because of another legal effect.
The spirit makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Cultivation Save DC.
On a failure, the Binding Seal takes hold.
On a success, the spirit resists and the Action or ritual is wasted, though the GM may allow partial containment for a scene.
While Binding Seal holds:
- the spirit cannot willingly move beyond the bond's range or vessel limits;
- the spirit cannot directly attack you unless the seal cracks;
- you may command limited service through Manifest the Spirit Nature;
- each coercive command that violates the spirit's Nature or Taboo increases Bond Strain by 1;
- the spirit may seek loopholes, sabotage, malicious compliance, or escape.
A Binding Seal is not friendship. It is a chain.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":83602,"source_global_line_start":83582,"source_heading":"Binding Seal","source_local_line_end":333,"source_local_line_start":313,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"Covenant Bond","exact_source_excerpt":"### Covenant Bond
A Covenant Bond is a willing relationship with a spirit.
The spirit must be willing, persuaded, repaid, rescued, honored, defeated honorably, inherited, or otherwise narratively available.
A Covenant Bond creates a Major Spirit Bond.
While the Covenant Bond remains stable:
- you and the spirit can communicate simple ideas while within 1 mile of each other;
- you always know the direction to the spirit while on the same plane or layer of reality;
- the spirit can be called, dismissed, or sheltered according to its Manifestation rules;
- the spirit may use Spirit Nature Expressions you have unlocked;
- you may make offerings to reduce Bond Strain;
- the spirit may refuse commands that violate its Nature, Need, or Taboo.
Covenant Bond is the default ethical mode of this sphere.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":83581,"source_global_line_start":83570,"source_heading":"Covenant Bond","source_local_line_end":312,"source_local_line_start":301,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"Manifestation Limits","exact_source_excerpt":"### Manifestation Limits
A spirit cannot use a Nature Expression if:
- the expression violates its core Nature;
- the spirit is sealed, asleep, banished, or suppressed;
- the host or vessel is broken;
- Bond Strain is at crisis and the GM rules the spirit refuses;
- the spirit's Taboo has just been violated;
- you cannot pay the required cost;
- the effect requires a legal target or origin the spirit does not have.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":83668,"source_global_line_start":83660,"source_heading":"Manifestation Limits","source_local_line_end":399,"source_local_line_start":391,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"Spirit Regard","exact_source_excerpt":"### Spirit Regard
When you successfully Read the Spirit Nature, you may place a Spirit Regard on the target.
Spirit Regard lasts for 1 hour, until you dismiss it, until the target is no longer on the same plane or layer of reality, or until the target hides its Nature with a stronger effect.
You have Advantage on the next Charisma, Wisdom, or Cultivation Check you make to communicate with, soothe, bargain with, bind, host, exorcise, or command a target bearing your Spirit Regard.
You may maintain a number of Spirit Regards equal to your Proficiency Bonus.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":83555,"source_global_line_start":83551,"source_heading":"Spirit Regard","source_local_line_end":286,"source_local_line_start":282,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"Temporary Scene Bond","exact_source_excerpt":"### Temporary Scene Bond
As an Action, you may spend 1 CP to create a temporary bond with a willing minor spirit, a spirit bearing your Spirit Regard, or a spirit whose Need you immediately satisfy.
The bond lasts for 1 scene.
During that scene, you may ask the spirit for one minor service, one piece of advice, one omen, one safe passage, one momentary manifestation, or one simple Nature Expression approved by the GM.
Temporary Scene Bonds do not count against your Major Spirit Bond limit unless the spirit fights for you or uses a major sphere effect.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":83629,"source_global_line_start":83625,"source_heading":"Temporary Scene Bond","source_local_line_end":360,"source_local_line_start":356,"structured_fields":{}}]

[{"component_name":"Wrestling Save DC and Escape DC","exact_source_excerpt":"#### Wrestling Save DC and Escape DC
Your default Wrestling Save DC and grapple escape DC are:
8 + Strength modifier + Proficiency Bonus
A Path synergy, Insight, or other feature may explicitly replace Strength for Wrestling talents or grapples created through this sphere.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":101094,"source_global_line_start":101091,"source_heading":"Wrestling Save DC and Escape DC","source_local_line_end":36,"source_local_line_start":33,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"Grappling Reminder","exact_source_excerpt":"#### Grappling Reminder
When you use the Grapple option of an Unarmed Strike:
choose one creature within 5 feet;
the target must be no more than one size larger than you;
you must have one hand or another eligible grappling body part free;
the target makes a Strength or Dexterity saving throw, choosing which;
on a failed save, it gains the Grappled condition.
While Grappled:
the target’s Speed is 0 and cannot increase;
the target has Disadvantage on attack rolls against creatures other than the grappler;
when the grappler drags or carries the target, each foot of movement costs 1 additional foot unless the target is Tiny or at least two sizes smaller than the grappler.
A Grappled creature may use its Action to make a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against the grapple’s escape DC, ending the condition on a success.
A grapple also ends if:
the grappler becomes Incapacitated;
the target leaves the grapple’s range;
the grappler releases the target without spending an Action.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":101110,"source_global_line_start":101095,"source_heading":"Grappling Reminder","source_local_line_end":52,"source_local_line_start":37,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"One Grapple per Hand or Body Part","exact_source_excerpt":"#### One Grapple per Hand or Body Part
One hand may maintain one grapple.
A feature may permit grappling through:
one hand;
two hands;
a weapon;
a tail;
a tentacle;
a maw;
another eligible body part.
Whatever part maintains the grapple cannot be used for another purpose unless a rule explicitly says otherwise.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":101121,"source_global_line_start":101111,"source_heading":"One Grapple per Hand or Body Part","source_local_line_end":63,"source_local_line_start":53,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"Applying a Slam","exact_source_excerpt":"#### Applying a Slam
When you learn Wrestling, choose one Slam talent for which you meet the prerequisites.
You may apply one Slam talent to one creature Grappled by you in any of the following ways:
##### Establish the Hold
When one creature gains the Grappled condition from your Unarmed Strike Grapple option or one of your Wrestling talents, use a Bonus Action to apply one Slam talent to that creature.
##### Work the Hold
When you begin your turn grappling one or more creatures, use a Bonus Action to apply one Slam talent to one creature Grappled by you.
##### Punish the Escape Attempt
When a creature fails an Action check to escape one of your grapples, use your Reaction to apply one Slam talent to it.
Unless a talent says otherwise:
one use applies one Slam talent;
the target must still be Grappled by you when the Slam resolves;
the Slam lasts until the start of your next turn or until the grapple ends, whichever happens first;
a Slam requiring a saving throw uses your Wrestling Save DC.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":101135,"source_global_line_start":101122,"source_heading":"Applying a Slam","source_local_line_end":77,"source_local_line_start":64,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"Special Attacks","exact_source_excerpt":"#### Special Attacks
When a Wrestling talent says it is a Special Attack, replace one attack when taking the Attack action unless the talent explicitly uses a different Action Type.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":101137,"source_global_line_start":101136,"source_heading":"Special Attacks","source_local_line_end":79,"source_local_line_start":78,"structured_fields":{}},{"component_name":"Restraints and Utilize","exact_source_excerpt":"#### Restraints and Utilize
The 2024 equipment rules give Rope, Chains, and Manacles their own binding rules.
When a Wrestling talent allows you to secure a creature with Rope, Chains, Manacles, or a similar restraint:
take the Utilize action unless the talent says otherwise;
satisfy the item’s normal requirements;
use the item’s normal escape and break rules unless the talent explicitly replaces them.","match_kind":"source_heading","source_global_line_end":101143,"source_global_line_start":101138,"source_heading":"Restraints and Utilize","source_local_line_end":85,"source_local_line_start":80,"structured_fields":{}}]
